# Root-level .dockerignore -- applies to every service whose docker-compose build
# context is the repo root (recruitment-workflow, resume-intelligence, second-brain;
# see infra/docker-compose.yml). VoiceHR builds from its own subdirectory context and
# is unaffected by this file.
#
# Primary reason this exists (see FRONTEND_HANDOFF.md §17): without it, every one of
# those three builds would upload the frontend's local node_modules/ (large,
# irrelevant to any Python image) and a stale local dist/ (rebuilt fresh by the
# Docker image's own Node build stage -- see services/recruitment-workflow/Dockerfile)
# as part of the build context, even though nothing ever COPYs them in that shape.

# Frontend build artifacts -- rebuilt fresh inside the Docker image itself
**/frontend/node_modules/
**/frontend/dist/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Env files -- passed to containers via docker-compose's env_file:, never COPYed
.env
.env.local
!.env.example

# VCS / editor / OS
.git/
.DS_Store

# VoiceHR's own runtime data (its build context doesn't include the repo root, but
# excluding it here too is harmless and keeps this file consistent with intent)
storage/recordings/
storage/transcripts/
*.db
